  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = (x - 6)^{2}\\). For what values of \\(x\\) is \\(f(x) = 25\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\) and \\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\) and \\(11\\)",
    "C": "\\(-11\\) and \\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\) only"
  },
  "answer": "B",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Set \\((x - 6)^{2} = 25\\). Taking square roots, \\(x - 6 = 5\\) or \\(x - 6 = -5\\).",
    "So \\(x = 11\\) or \\(x = 1\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Incorrect. From \\(x - 6 = -5\\), adding \\(6\\) gives \\(x = 1\\), not \\(-1\\).",
    "B": "Correct. \\((11 - 6)^{2} = 25\\) and \\((1 - 6)^{2} = (-5)^{2} = 25\\).",
    "C": "Incorrect. From \\(x - 6 = -5\\), \\(x = 1\\); and \\(-11\\) gives \\((-17)^{2} = 289\\), not \\(25\\).",
    "D": "Incorrect. \\(x - 6\\) can be \\(-5\\) as well as \\(5\\), since \\((-5)^{2} = 25\\); the second solution, \\(x = 1\\), is missing."
  },
  "traps": {
    "A": "sign_error",
    "C": "sign_error",
    "D": "stopped_early"
  },
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nsols = sorted(solve(Eq((x - 6)**2, 25), x))\nassert sols == [1, 11]\nassert choices[answer] == r'\\(1\\) and \\(11\\)'",
